        "content": "     1→{\n     2→  \"contentId\": \"test-ai-healthcare\",\n     3→  \"source\": {\n     4→    \"type\": \"text\",\n     5→    \"title\": \"The Future of AI in Healthcare\",\n     6→    \"url\": \"https://example.com/ai-healthcare\",\n     7→    \"creator\": \"Unknown\",\n     8→    \"publishedAt\": \"2024-12-08T00:00:00Z\"\n     9→  },\n    10→  \"summary\": {\n    11→    \"headline\": \"AI is fundamentally transforming healthcare through superior diagnostics, accelerated drug discovery, and personalized medicine.\",\n    12→    \"tldr\": \"AI-powered imaging detects cancers earlier than human radiologists with 95%+ accuracy while processing images in seconds versus minutes. It accelerates drug discovery from 10-15 years to much faster timelines and enables personalized medicine through genetic data analysis. Despite challenges around privacy, bias, and integration, AI will augment rather than replace doctors, with 60% of healthcare systems now implementing AI solutions.\",\n    13→    \"bullets\": [\n    14→      \"AI-powered imaging detects cancers earlier than human radiologists with 95%+ accuracy\",\n    15→      \"AI analyzes medical images in seconds vs. radiologist's 15 minutes, freeing experts for complex cases\",\n    16→      \"Drug discovery accelerates from 10-15 years through AI screening of molecular compounds\",\n    17→      \"Personalized medicine uses genetic data to predict disease risk and avoid adverse drug reactions\",\n    18→      \"Challenges include HIPAA compliance, training data bias, regulatory uncertainty, and system integration\",\n    19→      \"AI will augment rather than replace doctors, handling routine tasks while specialists focus on complex cases\",\n    20→      \"60% of healthcare systems are exploring/implementing AI solutions, up from 30% three years ago\"\n    21→    ],\n    22→    \"keyThemes\": [\n    23→      \"Diagnostic Revolution - AI outperforming humans in image analysis\",\n    24→      \"Efficiency Gains - Dramatic time savings in medical workflows\",\n    25→      \"Personalized Healthcare - Tailored treatments based on genetic data\",\n    26→      \"Human-AI Collaboration - Augmentation rather than replacement\",\n    27→      \"Ethical Challenges - Privacy, bias, and regulatory concerns\"\n    28→    ],\n    29→    \"importantQuotes\": [\n    30→      {\n    31→        \"text\": \"AI-powered imaging analysis can now detect certain cancers earlier than human radiologists.\",\n    32→        \"context\": \"Opening statement of Diagnostic Revolution section, establishing AI's superior capabilities\"\n    33→      },\n    34→      {\n    35→        \"text\": \"What might take a radiologist 15 minutes to analyze, an AI system can process in seconds, allowing radiologists to focus on complex cases and treatment planning rather than routine image analysis.\",\n    36→        \"context\": \"Explaining the efficiency advantage of AI in diagnostic workflows\"\n    37→      },\n    38→      {\n    39→        \"text\": \"AI enables truly personalized medicine by analyzing a patient's genetic data, medical history, lifestyle factors, and molecular markers.\",\n    40→        \"context\": \"Defining the comprehensive data analysis behind personalized medicine\"\n    41→      },\n    42→      {\n    43→        \"text\": \"Rather than replacing doctors, AI will augment medical professionals by handling routine diagnostic tasks, flagging unusual cases for specialist review, suggesting treatment options based on latest research, and monitoring patient outcomes to improve care.\",\n    44→        \"context\": \"Vision of collaborative human-AI healthcare future in The Path Forward section\"\n    45→      }\n    46→    ]\n    47→  },\n    48→  \"ideas\": {\n    49→    \"hooks\": [\n    50→      {\n    51→        \"text\": \"The day a machine saw my mother's cancer before her doctor did changed how I think about medicine forever.\",\n    52→        \"type\": \"emotional\"\n    53→      },\n    54→      {\n    55→        \"text\": \"What if the secret to curing cancer isn't in a lab, but in lines of code running on servers?\",\n    56→        \"type\": \"curiosity\"\n    57→      },\n    58→      {\n    59→        \"text\": \"AI isn't making medicine better - it's creating a healthcare system where machines make life-or-death decisions without human oversight.\",\n    60→        \"type\": \"controversy\"\n    61→      },\n    62→      {\n    63→        \"text\": \"A single AI system can analyze 10,000 medical images in the time it takes a radiologist to review one - and with 95% accuracy in cancer detection.\",\n    64→        \"type\": \"statistic\"\n    65→      },\n    66→      {\n    67→        \"text\": \"When Dr. Chen first saw the AI's diagnosis, she dismissed it as a computer error. Six months later, the biopsy proved the machine was right.\",\n    68→        \"type\": \"story\"\n    69→      }\n    70→    ],\n    71→    \"angles\": [\n    72→      {\n    73→        \"perspective\": \"The Patient's Dilemma\",\n    74→        \"approach\": \"Explore the tension between faster, more accurate diagnoses and loss of human connection in medicine through patient stories and ethical considerations.\",\n    75→        \"target\": \"General readers concerned about depersonalization of healthcare\",\n    76→        \"relevanceScore\": 0.8\n    77→      },\n    78→      {\n    79→        \"perspective\": \"The Overworked Doctor's Relief\",\n    80→        \"approach\": \"Focus on how AI alleviates burnout among medical professionals by handling routine tasks, featuring interviews with radiologists and surgeons.\",\n    81→        \"target\": \"Healthcare professionals and medical students\",\n    82→        \"relevanceScore\": 0.9\n    83→      },\n    84→      {\n    85→        \"perspective\": \"The Algorithm's Blind Spots\",\n    86→        \"approach\": \"Investigate cases where AI diagnostic tools failed due to biased training data, examining the real-world consequences for minority patients.\",\n    87→        \"target\": \"Tech ethicists, policymakers, and social justice advocates\",\n    88→        \"relevanceScore\": 0.7\n    89→      },\n    90→      {\n    91→        \"perspective\": \"The Startup Disruptor\",\n    92→        \"approach\": \"Profile AI healthcare startups racing to commercialize diagnostic tools, analyzing the billion-dollar market and regulatory hurdles.\",\n    93→        \"target\": \"Investors, entrepreneurs, and business readers\",\n    94→        \"relevanceScore\": 0.6\n    95→      },\n    96→      {\n    97→        \"perspective\": \"The Global Health Equalizer\",\n    98→        \"approach\": \"Document how AI tools are being deployed in rural clinics and developing nations to bridge healthcare gaps where specialists are scarce.\",\n    99→        \"target\": \"International development professionals and public health advocates\",\n   100→        \"relevanceScore\": 0.75\n   101→      }\n   102→    ],\n   103→    \"questions\": [\n   104→      {\n   105→        \"text\": \"How do we ensure AI diagnostic tools are trained on diverse patient data to avoid racial and gender bias?\",\n   106→        \"type\": \"analytical\",\n   107→        \"depth\": \"medium\"\n   108→      },\n   109→      {\n   110→        \"text\": \"What ethical framework should govern when an AI recommendation overrides a doctor's clinical judgment?\",\n   111→        \"type\": \"analytical\",\n   112→        \"depth\": \"deep\"\n   113→      },\n   114→      {\n   115→        \"text\": \"What specific steps can hospitals take this year to begin implementing AI diagnostic tools while maintaining patient trust?\",\n   116→        \"type\": \"practical\",\n   117→        \"depth\": \"surface\"\n   118→      },\n   119→      {\n   120→        \"text\": \"How should medical schools update their curriculum to prepare future doctors for AI-augmented practice?\",\n   121→        \"type\": \"practical\",\n   122→        \"depth\": \"medium\"\n   123→      },\n   124→      {\n   125→        \"text\": \"Does AI-assisted medicine fundamentally change what it means to be a healer, or is it just another tool in the medical toolkit?\",\n   126→        \"type\": \"philosophical\",\n   127→        \"depth\": \"deep\"\n   128→      },\n   129→      {\n   130→        \"text\": \"If AI can diagnose diseases earlier and more accurately, do doctors have an ethical obligation to use it despite potential risks?\",\n   131→        \"type\": \"philosophical\",\n   132→        \"depth\": \"deep\"\n   133→      },\n   134→      {\n   135→        \"text\": \"How does the adoption curve of AI in healthcare compare to previous medical revolutions like X-rays or antibiotics?\",\n   136→        \"type\": \"comparative\",\n   137→        \"depth\": \"medium\"\n   138→      },\n   139→      {\n   140→        \"text\": \"What can healthcare learn from other industries (like aviation or finance) about safely integrating AI into high-stakes decision making?\",\n   141→        \"type\": \"comparative\",\n   142→        \"depth\": \"medium\"\n   143→      }\n   144→    ]\n   145→  },\n   146→  \"suggestedOutline\": {\n   147→    \"title\": \"When Machines See Better Than Doctors: The AI Healthcare Revolution\",\n   148→    \"sections\": [\n   149→      {\n   150→        \"heading\": \"Introduction: The Diagnostic Disruption\",\n   151→        \"type\": \"intro\",\n   152→        \"points\": [\n   153→          \"Open with emotional hook about AI detecting cancer earlier than human doctors\",\n   154→          \"Establish the tension between technological promise and human expertise in medicine\",\n   155→          \"Preview the three main transformations: diagnostic imaging, drug discovery acceleration, and personalized medicine\",\n   156→          \"State the central question: Are we trading human connection for algorithmic accuracy?\"\n   157→        ],\n   158→        \"suggestedHook\":